WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Most products sold in the Amazon store are required to have an industry-standard unique product

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:13.000
ID number called a Global Trade Item Number or GTIN.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:20.500
This universal system, managed by Global Standards 1 or GS1, ensures accurate product identification

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:25.000
to help sort and track items across international marketplaces.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Each GTIN pairs with a unique barcode, which makes product IDs scannable.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:36.364
In most cases, you will need to provide a GTIN when you create a new product detail page in the

00:00:36.364 --> 00:00:37.000
Amazon store.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:43.667
A GTIN is also the surest way to match your offer to an existing product already sold in the Amazon

00:00:43.667 --> 00:00:44.000
store.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:50.892
If you match a listing using other information, like a brand or product name, Amazon will automatically

00:00:50.892 --> 00:00:57.784
associate your offer with the GTIN provided by the brand owner or brand qualified seller who first

00:00:57.784 --> 00:00:59.000
listed the product.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:05.000
Most product categories sold in the Amazon store require a specific type of GTIN.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:11.217
In many cases, it will be a 12-digit universal product code, UPC.

00:01:11.217 --> 00:01:18.870
Other accepted formats include the generic 14-digit GTIN, a 13-digit European article number, EAN,

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:27.000
a 13-digit Japanese article number, JAN, or a 10-13-digit international standard book number, ISBN.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:31.400
EANs and JANs are also sometimes referred to as international article numbers.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:38.000
You can often find a product's ID above or below the barcode on its packaging or shipping container.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:42.000
Each variation of a product will need to have its own product ID.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:47.649
For example, a small blue shirt will have a different product ID than the same blue shirt in medium,

00:01:47.649 --> 00:01:53.000
and a large green shirt will have a different product ID than the same large shirt in red.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:58.714
There are a few rare cases in which a product ID may not be required to create a product detail

00:01:58.714 --> 00:01:59.000
page.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:05.263
This could occur if you're selling a private label or handmade product for which the brand manufacturer

00:02:05.263 --> 00:02:11.526
or publisher does not provide a product ID, or if you're selling product parts or bundled products

00:02:11.526 --> 00:02:13.000
in a single pack.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:18.478
If your product is eligible for a GTIN exemption, you will be prompted to apply for an exemption

00:02:18.478 --> 00:02:20.000
during the listing setup process.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:28.312
To see if you meet the requirements for a GTIN exemption, search for list products that do not have

00:02:28.312 --> 00:02:34.000
a product ID, UPC, EAN, JAN, or ISBN help page in Seller Central.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:40.857
It's important to note that a GTIN is different from an Amazon standard identification number, ASIN,

00:02:40.857 --> 00:02:43.000
and stock keeping units, SKUs.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:49.538
An ASIN is an automatically assigned number used by Amazon to identify and track products in our

00:02:49.538 --> 00:02:56.462
catalog, and a SKU is a seller-specific number that can be used internally to help you identify

00:02:56.462 --> 00:02:58.000
and track your inventory.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:04.000
While all three numbers help different groups identify, track, buy, and sell products, only GTINs

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:10.000
are universal, and they're the number you'll use most often to list products on Amazon.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:17.000
To find category-specific product ID requirements before listing your products, search for GTIN

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:19.000
requirements on Seller Central.
